@page "/"

<PageTitle>Dashboard</PageTitle>

<section class="dashboard-hero">
    <div class="hero-content">
        <p class="dashboard-label">Fitness Nutrition Tracker</p>
        <h1>Personal Health Dashboard</h1>
        <p class="dashboard-description">
            Track meals, workouts, personal goals, and progress in one organized place.
            This dashboard connects the main features of the application and provides a clear starting point for the
            final demo.
        </p>

        <div class="dashboard-actions">
            <a class="btn btn-light btn-lg" href="nutrition-diary">Open Nutrition Diary</a>
            <a class="btn btn-outline-light btn-lg" href="workouts">Log Workout</a>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="hero-panel">
        <div class="hero-panel-card">
            <span class="hero-panel-label">Project Status</span>
            <strong>Ready for Review</strong>
            <p>Navigation, dashboard, profile, workouts, goals, and progress sections are connected for presentation.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="dashboard-stats">
    <div class="stat-card">
        <span class="stat-number">6</span>
        <span class="stat-label">Connected Sections</span>
    </div>

    <div class="stat-card">
        <span class="stat-number">Nutrition</span>
        <span class="stat-label">Meal Tracking</span>
    </div>

    <div class="stat-card">
        <span class="stat-number">Fitness</span>
        <span class="stat-label">Workout Records</span>
    </div>

    <div class="stat-card">
        <span class="stat-number">Goals</span>
        <span class="stat-label">Progress Planning</span>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section-heading">
    <p class="dashboard-label">Application Modules</p>
    <h2>Main Features</h2>
    <p>
        Use these sections to demonstrate how the project supports fitness tracking,
        nutrition planning, user profile management, goals, and progress review.
    </p>
</section>

<section class="feature-grid">

    <div class="feature-card">
        <div class="feature-icon">🥗</div>
        <h3>Nutrition Diary</h3>
        <p>
            Connects users to the nutrition area, including meal tracking, food search,
            nutrition records, and daily totals.
        </p>
        <a href="nutrition-diary">Go to Nutrition Diary</a>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-card">
        <div class="feature-icon">🏋️</div>
        <h3>Workouts</h3>
        <p>
            Allows users to add, edit, review, and delete workout records including type,
            duration, date, and notes.
        </p>
        <a href="workouts">Go to Workouts</a>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-card">
        <div class="feature-icon">👤</div>
        <h3>User Profile</h3>
        <p>
            Allows users to save and manage personal information such as name, age,
            height, and starting weight.
        </p>
        <a href="profile">Go to Profile</a>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-card">
        <div class="feature-icon">🎯</div>
        <h3>Goals</h3>
        <p>
            Provides a structured view of personal fitness and nutrition goals for planning
            and future expansion.
        </p>
        <a href="goals">Go to Goals</a>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-card">
        <div class="feature-icon">📈</div>
        <h3>Progress</h3>
        <p>
            Gives users a clear summary area for reviewing meals, workouts, completed goals,
            and overall progress.
        </p>
        <a href="progress">Go to Progress</a>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-card">
        <div class="feature-icon">✅</div>
        <h3>Demo Ready</h3>
        <p>
            The interface is organized for the final project presentation and connects the
            key pages created by the team.
        </p>
        <a href="progress">Review Progress</a>
    </div>

</section>